<article class="env-lemma" id="02NU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02NU">Lemma <span data-tag="02NU">29.45.10</span>.</a> A finite morphism is quasi-finite. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is implied by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00PM" data-tag="00PM">10.122.5</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/01TJ" data-tag="01TJ">29.21.9</a>. Alternatively, all points in fibres are closed points by Lemma <a href="/tag/02NT" data-tag="02NT">29.45.8</a> (and the fact that a finite morphism is integral) and use Lemma <a href="/tag/01TH" data-tag="01TH">29.21.6</a> (3) to see that $f$ is quasi-finite at $x$ for all $x \in X$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>